.TH SUPERSHOT 1 "2026-08-26" "supershot 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
supershot \- capture, annotate and share screenshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supershot
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SuperShot
is a native GTK4/Libadwaita screenshot tool for Linux desktops.
.PP
Captures are taken through the XDG Desktop Portal on both Wayland and X11.
When no portal backend answers, SuperShot falls back to whichever command-line
screenshot tool the session provides: on Wayland
.BR grim (1)
with
.BR slurp (1),
.BR spectacle (1),
.B wayshot
or
.BR hyprshot ;
on X11
.BR gnome-screenshot (1),
.BR xfce4-screenshooter (1),
.BR spectacle (1),
.BR scrot (1),
.BR maim (1),
.BR flameshot (1)
or ImageMagick's
.BR import (1).
.PP
Running without options opens the graphical interface. With
.B \-\-now
the capture is taken and the program exits, which suits keyboard shortcuts and
scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delay " " \fISECONDS\fR
Wait this many seconds before capturing. Default 0.
.TP
.B \-\-now
Capture without showing the graphical interface, then exit. The path of the
saved file is printed to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
What to capture:
.BR interactive " (let the capture backend ask), "
.BR area ", " window " or " screen .
Default
.BR interactive .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format:
.BR png " (default), " jpeg " or " jpg .
.TP
.BR \-\-quality " " \fIN\fR
JPEG encoder quality from 1 to 100. Default 90. Ignored for PNG.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Save into this directory instead of the configured location.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-edit " " \fIFILE\fR
Open the annotation editor on an existing image instead of capturing a new one.
No screenshot backend is involved.
.TP
.B \-\-watermark
Overlay the configured date/time watermark.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH "KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS"
.TP
.B Ctrl+Enter
Take a screenshot.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.PP
In the preview window:
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Undo the last annotation or crop.
.TP
.BR "Ctrl+Shift+Z" ", " Ctrl+Y
Redo.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Render the annotated image to the clipboard without writing a file.
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel the pending selection.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/Screenshots/
Default save location, overridable in the Settings tab or with
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.I ~/.config/glib-2.0/settings/keyfile
Where GSettings persists preferences on systems without dconf.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPERSHOT_DEBUG_LAYOUT
Report the preview window's widget geometry to standard output and exit. Set it
to \fIWIDTHxHEIGHT\fR to resize the window first, for inspecting how the
sidebar adapts.
.TP
.B SUPERSHOT_LOCALEDIR
Override the directory searched for compiled translation catalogs. Normally
resolved from the installation prefix.
.TP
.B GDK_BACKEND
Force the windowing backend. SuperShot selects its fallback screenshot tools
from the backend GDK actually connected to, so forcing
.B x11
inside a Wayland session correctly enables the X11 helpers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Capture an area after three seconds and save it as JPEG:
.EX
supershot \-\-now \-\-mode area \-\-delay 3 \-\-format jpeg \-\-quality 85
.EE
.TP
Capture the whole screen into a specific directory:
.EX
supershot \-\-now \-\-mode screen \-\-output ~/Documents/shots
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR grim (1),
.BR slurp (1),
.BR gnome-screenshot (1),
.BR spectacle (1),
.BR scrot (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/axpnet/supershot/issues
.SH AUTHOR
axpnet <axp@pm.me>
